      "statement": "AXION's TLP engines emit requests using only the 4-DW (64-bit address) header form and the DUT rejects the 3-DW form, so request payload always starts on a beat boundary; completion headers are genuinely 3 DW but padded to 4 DW with one reserved DW to keep completion payload beat-aligned as a stream-packing convention, not a header field change.",
